@startuml overview
' cumin-works - when cumin notifies. Each cause is notified once.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

left to right direction

rectangle "a person needs to decide\n(an awaiting- state)" as Decide
rectangle "something is wrong\n(no permission, no Assignee, an unreadable issue,\nan unread usage, a failed tool check,\nno ruleset, failed polls)" as Wrong
rectangle "a usage reaches its threshold" as Limit
rectangle "no issue cumin can move on" as Waits

rectangle "notify once:\na link and one line of the reason" as Notify
rectangle "the issue and the pull request\nhold the details and the talk" as GitHub

Decide --> Notify
Wrong --> Notify
Limit --> Notify
Waits --> Notify
Notify --> GitHub : the reader goes to

@enduml
